":"10e64c7a","settings":{"title":"Solving Common AC Problems Before They Lead To Bigger Repairs ","align":"center","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Como-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":60,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"px","size":40,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"800","typography_text_transform":"capitalize","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.1000000000000001,"sizes":[]},"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"279d6a3"}],"_animation":"zoomIn","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=primary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6326c7d5","settings":{"editor":"<p>Air conditioners rarely fail without warning. In many cases, your system will show signs of stress before it shuts down completely. Catching these problems early can help you avoid larger repairs, higher energy bills, and uncomfortable downtime during the hottest months of the year.<\/p>","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"BeVietnamPro-Light","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"10","right":"10","bottom":"10","left":"10","isLinked":true},"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"ab32aea"}],"__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4b68ee6d","settings":{"editor":"<p>At Magnolia Air, we repair a wide range of AC issues, including:<\/p><ul><li>Air conditioner blowing warm air<\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/magnoliaairllc.com\/troubleshooting-poor-airflow-from-ac-vents\/\">Weak or inconsistent airflow<\/a><\/li><li>Unusual noises such as grinding, buzzing, rattling, or clanking<\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/magnoliaairllc.com\/common-causes-of-ac-water-leaks\/\">Water leaking<\/a> around the indoor unit<\/li><li>Frequent cycling on and off<\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/magnoliaairllc.com\/ways-to-lower-energy-bill-summer\/\">Rising energy bills<\/a><\/li><li>Frozen evaporator coils<\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/magnoliaairllc.com\/how-to-fix-ac-thermostat-problems\/\">Thermostat problems<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"https:\/\/magnoliaairllc.com\/ac-refrigerant-leaks-warning-signs\/\">Refrigerant leaks<\/a><\/li><li>Electrical issues or breaker trips<\/li><li>Systems that will not start or will not stay running<\/li><\/ul>","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"BeVietnamPro-Light","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400","_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"10","right":"10","bottom":"10","left":"10","isLinked":true},"display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"ab32aea"}],"__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"28b162d7","settings":{"editor":"<p>Some symptoms are more urgent than others. Warm air may point to refrigerant issues, compressor trouble, or airflow restrictions. Water around the unit may indicate a clogged drain line or frozen coil. Burning smells, repeated breaker trips, or electrical issues should be handled right away to help prevent safety risks or more serious system damage.<\/p><p>Our trained technicians look beyond the surface symptom to identify what is actually causing the problem, then explain your repair options clearly.<\/p>","display_condition_list":[{"display_condition_login_status":"subscriber","_id":"b564100"}]},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"42eef626","settings":{"text":"Request Service","align":"justify","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"BeVietnamPro-ExtraBold","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px",